## goods. Built lazily with the NPC tables.
var _shop_reader: ShopReader = null
## The teleport network's tables (TeleportReader, round 577): which gate
## structures stand in a region (_bind_region_gates) and what a gate offers
## (_npc_services). Built with the NPC tables.
var _teleport_reader: TeleportReader = null
var _npc_tables_loaded := false
## The NPC whose talk box is open, so a chosen service (Buy, ...) knows who it
## is for.
var _talk_npc_name := ""
var _talk_npc_code := ""
## The player's guild as the server last reported it, for the guild NPC's
## talk lines (NpcServiceReader.guild_services, round 521): -1 until a guild
## reply arrives (the NPC then keeps the "Guild" placeholder), 0 for no
## guild, else the guild's id. _guild_master is whether the player leads it.
## It can go stale: the server sends no guild broadcasts (session/guild.go
## answers only the requester), so only this player's own replies move it.
## When the leader leaves, guild.Store.Leave hands leadership to the
## longest-standing member, who is not told -- that client keeps
## _guild_master false and still offers "Leave guild." until its next
## guild_info reply (world entry, or opening the guild window). Only a refused
## leave asks the server again (_on_guild_leave_result).
var _guild_id := -1
var _guild_master := false
## The guild's points as the server last reported them (round 525), for the
## Guild tab: _guild_gathered_sp is the guild's GatheredSP (-1 until an
## OpGuildPoints reply for _guild_id arrives) and _guild_donations maps each
## member's name to its GP_Donation. _on_guild_result asks for them after
## every successful reply for a guild, and _guild_roster is that reply, kept
## so the points reply can redraw the tab. Like _guild_id, they move only on
## this player's own replies: the server pushes nothing when points are
